<title>RUSSIA: Two more mutual funds registered in Russia.</title>
<headline>Two more mutual funds registered in Russia.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main securities watchdog the Federal Commission for the Securities Market registered the rules and prospectuses of Open Mutual Fund for Short-Term Hard Currency Investments and Credis Open Mutual Fund for Investment in Large Companies' Shares, the commission said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>OAO Credis (Moscow) A/O, part of CS Holding's Credit Suisse, is the managing company for both funds.</p>
<p>The new funds, similar to British unit trusts or U.S. mutual funds, are the third and fourth to be registered in Russia, following PIF Pioner Pervy and Pallada Government Securities Unit Investment Fund.</p>
<p>--Olga Popova, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
